    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\nInterested in this property? Sign up for mySherryFitz to arrange your viewing, see current offers or make your own offer. Register now at SherryFitz.ie.\n\nThis charming former Parochial House enjoys a peaceful and scenic country setting in the heart of the village of Abbey, while being conveniently located just c.18km from Loughrea Town and all its amenities. \n\nAlthough requiring refurbishment, the property offers an exciting opportunity for the discerning purchaser to transform and renovate the residence to their own taste and style.\nExtending to approximately 129.4 m², the accommodation comprises three bedrooms, sitting room, kitchen and bathroom, offering excellent potential to create a wonderful family home or country retreat. \n\nViewing is highly recommended and can be arranged by appointment through the selling agent."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "\nEntry - 1.69m x 2.17m\nDual aspect windows, tile flooring\n\nHallway - 1.83m x 5.47m\nFront aspect door, tiled flooring\n\nSitting Room - 4.05m x 5.40m\nDual aspect windows, solid fuel stove with ornate wooden surround, carpet flooring\n\nKitchen Dining Room - 3.73m x 5.40m\nDual aspect windows, wall and base units, solid fuel range, vinyl and carpet flooring\n\nUtility Room - 2.36m x 1.15m\nDoor to rear, tile flooring\n\nStorage - 2.37m x 1.15m\nRear aspect window\n\nFirst Floor - \n\n\nLanding - 1.85m x 2.71m\nFront aspect window, carpet flooring\n\nBedroom 1 - 3.89m x 5.47m\nDual aspect windows, solid fuel fireplace and surround, shower unit, carpet flooring\n\nBedroom 2 - 4.19m x 3.35m\nDual aspect windows, carpet flooring\n\nBedroom 3 - 4.23m x 1.99m\nRear aspect window, carpet flooring\n\nBathroom - 2.29m x 1.76m\nRear aspect window, whb/wc/electric shower, fitted storage, tiled floor\n\nGarden - \nLarge mature garden, long driveway, garden laid to lawn, patio area and various outbuildings\n\n"
      },
